   "text": "“They were trying to find ways to take it off us,” he said of the disputed decisions.\nSections of the 48,000-strong crowd at Eden Park were fuming and beer cans and bottles were thrown towards referee Ashley Klein at full-time. Bunker official Chris Butler was, in fact, at the heart of the controversies.\nThe first incident in the 73rd minute was ruled as a knock-on from Knights centre Bradman Best",
